From b52fa52a21c3378f0ddc953e27c4182f2734fefa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lichtenshtein <altruumann@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 03:32:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] theogbob's ffmpeg-hvqm2 fork changes

https://github.com/theogbob/ffmpeg-hvqm2

Adds read/write support for Hudson's HVQM2 1.0 video format — the .hvqm container used on the Nintendo 64 (Hybrid Vector Quantization, the codec behind games' full-motion video).

The original Hudson toolchain shipped a slow Windows-only encoder (hvqm2enc.exe). This fork replaces it with a fast, native FFmpeg encoder plus a complete container implementation, so you can produce and play .hvqm files with the standard ffmpeg/ffprobe tools on any platform.

