 Default value is 0.
 @end table
 
+@section hvqm
+Hudson HVQM2 (@code{.hvqm}) demuxer.
+
+This demuxer reads the HVQM2 1.0 container used on the Nintendo 64, exposing its
+@code{hvqm2} video stream and, when present, its mono @code{adpcm_ima_hvqm2}
+audio stream. FFmpeg ships an HVQM2 audio decoder but no HVQM2 @emph{video}
+decoder, so video packets can be identified and stream-copied but not decoded.
+
 @section image2
 
 Image file demuxer.
diff --git a/doc/encoders.texi b/doc/encoders.texi
index 605638e..b77a728 100644
--- a/doc/encoders.texi
+++ b/doc/encoders.texi
@@ -1503,6 +1503,37 @@ Default value is @option{snappy}.
 
 @end table
 
+@section HVQM2
+
+Hudson HVQM2 (Hybrid Vector Quantization) video encoder, the codec used by the
+@code{.hvqm} container on the Nintendo 64. It accepts @code{yuv420p} ("4:1:1",
+2x2 chroma) and @code{yuv422p} input; dimensions must be multiples of 8, at
+least 144x80 and at most 640x480.
+
+@subsection Options
+
+@table @option
+@item quality @var{integer}
+Matching-pursuit threshold @var{Z} (Hudson's @code{-q}). Higher values use fewer
+Adaptive Orthogonal Transform basis vectors, giving smaller, blockier frames.
+Default is 400.
+
+@item me_range @var{integer}
+Motion-estimation search range in pixels for inter (P) frames (Hudson's
+@code{-r}), from 0 to 63. @code{0} disables motion (zero-vector only). Default
+is 32.
+
+@item scene @var{integer}
+Scene-change keyframe sensitivity (Hudson's @code{-a}), from 0 to 100. @code{0}
+makes every frame a keyframe; @code{100} never inserts a scene-change keyframe.
+In between, a keyframe is inserted when more than @var{scene} percent of the
+macroblocks are poorly motion-compensated. Default is 80.
+@end table
+
+The keyframe interval is set with the generic @option{-g} option (Hudson's
+@code{-k}); the HVQM2 default is 30. @code{-g 0} disables periodic keyframes,
+leaving only scene-change keyframes.
+
 @section jpeg2000
 
 The native jpeg 2000 encoder is lossy by default, the @code{-q:v}
diff --git a/doc/muxers.texi b/doc/muxers.texi
index 03f0bcd..286d8af 100644
--- a/doc/muxers.texi
+++ b/doc/muxers.texi
@@ -2537,6 +2537,15 @@ Ignore IO errors during open, write and delete. Useful for long-duration runs wi
 Set custom HTTP headers, can override built in default headers. Applicable only for HTTP output.
 @end table
 
+@section hvqm
+Hudson HVQM2 (@code{.hvqm}) muxer.
+
+This muxer writes the HVQM2 1.0 container used on the Nintendo 64: a big-endian
+file header followed by interleaved video and audio records. It takes one
+@code{hvqm2} video stream and, optionally, one mono @code{adpcm_ima_hvqm2} audio
+stream. The output must be seekable, as the header's record counters are
+backfilled when the trailer is written.
+
 @section iamf
 Immersive Audio Model and Formats (IAMF) muxer.
 
